# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the memory-integrity sanitizer build
# (docs/prd-memory-integrity-tests.md §3.3, §9.8).
#
# Format (one per line):
#   leak:<substring matched against a frame in the leak's stack trace>
#
# Usage (wired by .github/workflows/memory-tests.yml and
# scripts/check-release.sh):
#   LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=$PWD/cedar/tests/lsan.supp
#
# RULES (enforced by review; §9.8 flags stale entries at release time):
#   * Every entry MUST carry a one-line comment explaining WHAT leaks and
#     WHY it is acceptable (third-party library, intentional one-shot leak
#     during static init, etc.).
#   * Never suppress a leak in cedar/ or akkado/ runtime code to make the
#     build green. A real leak is a finding — fix it, don't mute it.
#   * Stale entries (matching no symbol on the current build) are reviewed
#     and removed at each release.
#
# No suppressions are needed at present — the suite runs leak-clean.
